{
  "_comment": "The battery strikes (exe patch 143, docs/notes/battery-hit.md): the ram (both arms push the battery out) and the shove (the right arm drives its right end forward about the left hand), authored on the stock rig (scripts/battery-hit: swing.py's keys, make_clips.py writes them) as the game plays a battery state: its player clips move the carrier's shoulders and arms alone (bone mask 2), its battery clips the battery by its own offset bone. The battery's states 3 to 6, a swing (the gather and the drive, ending on the strike, the battery at its fastest) and a recovery (the follow-through, the settle and the way back to the carry idle) for each: 3 and 4 the ram's, 5 and 6 the shove's, which the cook loads as it loads states 0 to 2. The states are known by their index, as the game reads them (the cook's states[0] take_time, states[2] put_time; the machine's order).",
